d have  several dress pants but for me i'm just  a dress kind of a girl i like skirts and  dresses so one dress pant that is black  that fits with different things is all  that i need i also like that it's  high-waisted and it's a thin material so  i love it in the summer because it's  just it doesn't feel hot but in the  winter i can put my leggings underneath  and just be so warm and toasty and  nobody would ever know next up on the  list is a summer hat and truly i only  wear this about one or two times a year  when we go to the beach so if we were  talking about how much i use it some  people could probably say that i  shouldn't own it but you know what i  like it i think it's pretty i feel good  when i'm wearing it and so for me it's  okay to keep this even though i only  wear it a couple of times throughout the  year but that being said because i don't  wear hats often i don't need more than  one i can only justify having one for  myself next up on the list is a hair  scrunchie so i actually have this brand  it's by teletize and i tried this  because i have long hair and my hair  would always hurt when putting it up in  a ponytail so i heard about this brand  people were raving about it and i tried  it to see if it would actually keep my  ponytail up without hurting my hair and  actually i was surprised that it did i  did like the way that it held my hair up  this is the only scrunchie that i have  now and it works perfectly for me if  they stretch out i can just put it in  hot water and it kind of like shrinks  back to size so  now i don't have all sorts of the black  hair ties i can just use the one  and the last item on this list that i  only own one of is an umbrella and this  is actually one that i'd like your  advice on so to give you some backstory  my husband and i we kind of both come  from the country from mexico and he was  kind of raised that even if it's raining  you go out and you work and  when he was young he had to work before  he went to school and then after school  now i was young i didn't really have  that experience um but when we got  married he just kind of instilled in to  me that even if it rained it didn't  matter he was going out and working  outside and and i liked that i actually  liked that because  i kind of grew up with this oh it's  raining i can't go outside i can't do  the things that i would do if it's not  raining and  so i started to adopt that and truly  where we live we don't have a garage we  just we go out we take the kids in the  vehicle if we get wet we get wet i mean  don't get me wrong they have rain boots  and they have rain jackets but for me  i don't own rain boots or rain jackets  and you know what if i get wet i get wet  it's okay so i actually rarely use the  umbrella and i'd kind of like for our  kids to  not be afraid of the elements like be  well dressed and be prepared but it's  okay if it's raining go out go have fun  go do work go do whatever it is that  you're gonna go do so i don't know i'm  kind of thinking of actually  decluttering the umbrella what do you  think should we declutter it is that  actually a necessity what's your point  of view on this okay i need to move on  with this list because i feel like i'm  ranting on forever but now moving on to  the items that i don't own  first up pajamas i am probably gonna  drive some elegant women out there crazy  because i don't own pajamas for a while  i was using a slip that i used under my  dresses as my pajama and then that had  seen better days it was time to let it  go  and i just never replaced it you know  what if i wear a t-shirt i wear a  t-shirt it's fine i think confidence  looks much better on a person than what  you own and what you're actually wearing  on the exterior so for me  i don't feel like i need pajamas i'm  okay  next item that i do not own is swimsuits  so i mentioned that i have one pair of  shorts and it's like quick drying  material i realized that i had several  swimsuits and  i don't 