at these things have  chemicals called endocrine disruptors  and what these things do is they  actually harm your body's natural  processes and they have been linked to  cancer and for individuals with cancer  there is worry that these could actually  cause worsening of the condition  so just kind of do your research on  scented items they are horrible things  they're really toxic for you they're not  things that you really want to be  breathing in so what i did is i got rid  of all those sorts of things now if i  ever want perfume  essential oils is what i use but i do  not use those sorts of things in my  house and if anything what i did is  bring in more plants specifically air  purifying plants because these clean the  air nasa actually recommends that you  have one air purifying plant per every  100 square feet you have in your home so  i started to bring in more plants in the  home like the san severia or the snake  plant pothos just different plants that  clean the air and just allow my home to  have  healthy air to breathe the next item  that i don't own is conditioner like  hair conditioner and so as i started to  learn about scented items and scented  lotions and perfumes and that sort of  thing it kind of brought me the question  well what else is toxic in my home and  believe me there was a huge list of  things that i slowly started to get rid  of as my eyes were just opened up and  one of the things that i learned about  was the toxic chemicals that are often  placed in shampoos and conditioners and  i learned about coconut oil oh there's  gotta be a bajillion uses for coconut  oil but i started using it as a hair  conditioner basically what i do is i use  it as a hair mask before i shampoo and  this is not an everyday thing it's  really once i start to see my hair kind  of getting dry i put it on my hair and  my scalp as a mask about 30 minutes  before i go into the shower and then i  shampoo like normally and this leaves my  hair feeling soft i have not really  needed conditioners anymore also another  thing that i just thought of that is not  included on the list but i don't have  teeth whiteners because coconut oil is  also good for oil pulling basically i  used to have teeth whiteners which were  horrible for your teeth and they made my  teeth hurt actually and now what i do is  i just kind of swish around coconut oil  in my mouth if you want to add baking  soda even better and it makes your teeth  white  coconut oil has a bajillion uses guys  you don't need teeth whiteners the next  item on the list is an assortment again  it's all sorts of skin paraphernalia  like toners and skin cleansers and  anti-aging things and shaving creams all  those sorts of things i do not use any  of those if anything i have minimized so  much because now i just use a coconut  oil bar soap to wash my face and if my  skin is dry i just kind of follow up  with just a dab of coconut oil it does  it for me because i never really noticed  any of those other things doing magical  things for me and believe me i was at  the age of 20 buying anti-aging serums  and things like that that  i didn't need  and lastly but certainly not least the  number one item that really changed a  lot of things for us when we decluttered  it is the television i never really  liked the tv anyway but when my husband  decided that we were gonna get rid of  the tv  i was all for it let me give you the  back story my husband and i have been  very much in love from the very  beginning we are super cheesy we are  very happy couple but we did have a  problem especially as newlyweds really  as newlyweds um is that he was very much  addicted to video games he'll be the  first person to admit it i would come  home from work i'm a nurse so 12 hour  shifts and  when i would arrive he would be on the  screen playing his video game you guys  he wouldn't even turn to look at me to  say hello how are you how was your day  he would keep on playing uh-huh yes  honey  he wouldn't join me at the dinner table  because he had to finish that level  sometimes i'd go to bed at night and he  would be playing that game because he he  just had to get to that one last level  it was an addiction it was a true  addiction and when i got pregnant with  our first child something just changed  within him it was like he realized that  we had a problem and that it was not  okay don't get me wrong he is an amazing  amazing man who serves me he gets up in  the morning and makes me breakfast even  though he gets up at four in the morning  i mean he is truly serving me and and  does care for me however this one thing  had to change and he was willing to  change that  and so i was surprised when one day he  calls me up and he says  get rid of that tv sell it donate it  whatever i don't want it in the house  i've gotten rid of the console i don't  want it anymore i just about wanted to  cry that day i was like  okay  i'm not going to give you time to change  your mind about it we're getting rid of  it  and i was surprised when after i got rid  of it i thought i thought there would be  like this morning period where he would  be like what am i gonna do and and no  actually none of that when we started  this minimalist journey i never really  forced him to get rid of anything i  didn't make him you got to get rid of  these things um i started to get rid of  my own things and as i did that i  started to see changes in him he started  to see that we could work together  towards our goals and that kind of also  at the same time started to  impact our financial goals this is when  we started to know about dave ramsey and  the fire movement and we started to  really work hard on our goals our mutual  goals so instead of having the tv it  wasn't this morning period we now had  time to work together towards our future  and  matter of fact we had a lot of work to  do because we built this house i mean  our names are written in the studs we  did this and we did this together and i  think in huge part because we didn't  have this tv as a distraction we now  have the time to work more but for a  greater purpose for something together  in unity now tv may not be an addiction  for you that is okay if you have this  this item but for us it was causing  problems and so he decided to get rid of  it nail it kind of like i got rid of my  nail polish because it was a problem for  me i got rid of my prom dresses because  that was a problem for me so really see  the items that are not helping you get  to where you want to be keep the items  that are helping you towards that goal  if you have for example tools for  construction or mechanic tools and and  that's going to help you get to where  you want to be keep those don't get rid  of those but any items that you have  that are holding you back from achieving  your goals from achieving your dreams  those are really the items that you  should be tackling so it really doesn't  matter if you have one less spoon or one  less fork  because there's something bigger that  you know that you need to be  decluttering so my hope for all of this  is not that you really look at  individual items  more so that you look at your life in  entirety what kind of a life do you want  to have and what kind of items do you  picture yourself having with that ideal  life and what items are helping you get  to that life and what items are  hindering you from getting to that point  so just kind of take a look at those  hopefully this list has been helpful for  you please know this is not something  that you have to get rid of all those  things it's just meant as an idea  hopefully some inspiration i hope it's  been enjoyable i thank you for your time  and i can't wait to hear from you in the  comments and let me know about that  umbrella thing i really want to know  what you think so thank you for your  time i can't wait to hear from you until  next time  bye
 

